+# Shared replay integrity correction
+
+Reviewed and corrected on 14 October 2026 by Codex (automated).
+Application version: 0.4.4; the corrected source has new replay fingerprints.
+
+## Reproduced defect and correction
+
+The shared comparison helper accepted positive or negative infinity as
+matching a finite reading, because both sides of its relative allowance
+could become infinite. It also treated Boolean flags as numeric 0/1.
+A malformed enormous integer could raise OverflowError during comparison.
+
+Actual native incident generation and replay in separate source processes
+reproduced these outcomes. The saved source accepted both infinities and a
+numeric feasibility flag, and crashed on the enormous integer. Corrected
+source returns an unmatched result for all four, with no exception.
+[Before/after reproduction](verification/replay-fix-2026-10-14/reproduction.json).
+
+The shared helper now rejects non-finite numbers on either side and requires
+Boolean flags to remain Boolean. Equal finite integers retain their identity;
+overflow during malformed numeric comparison reports a difference. Existing
+finite-value relative tolerances are retained. These checks apply to every
+replay/evidence path using the shared helper, including incident, regression,
+episode, temporal, failure-search and defect comparisons.
+
+Twenty-three new regressions cover both operand sides, nested readings,
+infinities/NaN, Boolean/numeric substitution, unchanged finite tolerance,
+large integers and actual native incident replay. Regression and episode
+exports with deliberately recomputed checksums still reject altered flag
+types. The diagnostic study now fingerprints the shared comparison source
+as an explicit dependency.
+
+## Evidence and source identity
+
+Changing service.py changes core, search, harness, assurance and episode
+fingerprints. Earlier records retain their original identities and are not
+relabelled as executions of the corrected source. The saved checkpoint
+`GridSense_Release_Prepared_v2.zip` has SHA-256
+`8dccbb8d170d7ee01155ee16625df31522a01c49f41a941fd86ffd28768898aa`.
+It preserves complete previous source, studies and protocols. Its full
+verification is also archived under
+[checkpoint checks](verification/evidence-input-2026-10-14/checkpoint-checks/verification.json).
+
+Original protocols are retained in
+`experiments/protocols/archive/replay-fix-2026-10-14/`. Quality, assurance
+and measurement-refresh protocols receive explicit revision/source pins;
+challenge and native-reuse freezes capture the corrected source and retain
+their predecessor hashes. All cases, seeds, budgets, variants, tolerances
+and analysis settings remain unchanged.
+[Protocol/source revision record](verification/replay-fix-2026-10-14/protocol-revision.json).
+
+Nine affected studies are executed anew: controller grid, paired search,
+transfer, fixed-seed quality evaluation, fault injection, restoration
+sessions, boundary challenge, measurement refresh and native reuse. Original
+study results remain in the preserved checkpoint; the current experiment
+directories contain new executions with matching source fingerprints.
+[Execution record](verification/replay-fix-2026-10-14/study-runs.json).
+Independent study processes overlap, so their wall times are not suitable
+for speed comparisons with previous runs.
+
+Bundled portable examples are generated again from the same saved requests
+and definitions, then strictly replayed. The reference sensitivity study is
+regenerated with its explicit comparison-helper dependency. Electrical model
+inputs and algorithms are unchanged; the original scientific reference
+remains 52/56 under native defaults.
+
+## Verification and delivery
+
+The complete Linux verification, including all study identity/accounting
+checks, browser workflows, real native runtime and restart recovery, is
+recorded in [current verification](VERIFICATION.md). The release packager
+requires complete successful software checks, matching input/build bytes,
+ZIP CRCs and per-file hashes. Earlier verification and review records retain
+their own dated scope.
+
+The [incremental source patch](reviews/replay-integrity-2026-10-14.patch)
+applies to the saved checkpoint. Updated study data and verification are
+supplied in the complete ZIP; rerun affected studies and verification after
+applying a source-only patch.
+
+Windows execution, GitHub-hosted CI, independent software/power-systems
+reviews and owner license selection remain pending. This correction does
+not add shared-network authentication, protection dynamics or field-grid
+validation.
